# No raw host IPs in this repo

**This repository is public.** Never write the VPS / match-host origin IP address
(or any other server IP) into tracked files — code, config, `.htaccess`, scripts,
docs, comments, or commit messages. That applies even to lines that are commented
out or gated behind a marker file.

Address the match host by name or by an overridable variable instead:

```bash
# ❌ BAD — origin IP literal in a public file
VPS_HOST="${VPS_HOST:-root@203.0.113.10}"
curl "http://203.0.113.10:5003/api.php?action=ping"

# ✅ GOOD — hostname default, operator can override
VPS_HOST="${VPS_HOST:-root@stream.loveliveradio.ca}"
ssh "$VPS_HOST" "curl -fsS 'http://127.0.0.1:5003/api.php?action=ping'"
```

- Public HTTP endpoints: use `https://stream.loveliveradio.ca/tcg/api` (its nginx
  TLS front), never `http://<ip>:<port>`.
- Loopback (`127.0.0.1`) and container service names (`redis`) are fine.
- Anything that must carry a real address belongs in a gitignored operator file
  (`.env.deploy`, `tcg_sync.local.php`) or an environment variable.
- Same for user-visible client code: `client/js/**` and `index.html` may only
  reference public hostnames.
